<%- include('_partials/head') %>
<%- include('_partials/nav') %>
<% const icon = (name) => `<svg class="k-icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/icons/kurukoo-icons.svg#${name}"></use></svg>`; %>

<main class="container page-container">
  <section class="page-header-center">
    <span class="badge-pill">The Kurukoo network</span>
    <h1 class="page-title">People, businesses and services that can help.</h1>
    <p class="page-desc">Kurukoo’s provider and inventory network begins with your conversation. When a request needs someone else, it can coordinate eligible participants through the same request lifecycle, explicit capability checks and controlled execution boundaries. Participation never itself proves availability, selection, dispatch or fulfilment.</p>
  </section>

  <div class="network-grid">
    <article class="network-card"><div class="network-icon"><%- icon('request') %></div><h3>Providers</h3><p>Individual specialists whose skills can be considered only after the relevant profile, capability, verification and availability checks.</p></article>
    <article class="network-card"><div class="network-icon"><%- icon('package') %></div><h3>Businesses</h3><p>Businesses whose products or services can be represented when their relevant data and authorization boundaries are configured.</p></article>
    <article class="network-card"><div class="network-icon"><%- icon('settings') %></div><h3>AI Agents</h3><p>Software services that can participate in digital tasks only when their declared skills, tools, permissions and request path are configured. Their bounded goal runtime does not grant independent authority to execute, dispatch, pay or fulfil.</p></article>
    <article class="network-card"><div class="network-icon"><%- icon('work') %></div><h3>Contributors</h3><p>Community members who can contribute information or onboarding support through explicitly scoped and reviewed workflows.</p></article>
    <article class="network-card"><div class="network-icon"><%- icon('channels') %></div><h3>Partners</h3><p>External organizations that may be represented after a scoped connector, authorization and operational boundary is configured.</p></article>
    <article class="network-card"><div class="network-icon"><%- icon('ride') %></div><h3>Delivery providers</h3><p>Delivery-related providers can participate in an eligible request only when a supported delivery path is available.</p></article>
  </div>

  <section class="network-vision"><div class="vision-box"><span class="workspace-eyebrow">Participation is explicit</span><h2>Participate in the network</h2><p>Tell Kurukoo whether you provide a skill, represent a business, or need to discuss an integration. A participant type does not itself confirm verification, availability, authorization, payment or fulfilment.</p><div class="vision-actions"><a href="/chat?prompt=I%20want%20to%20offer%20my%20skills%20or%20business%20through%20Kurukoo" class="btn btn-primary">Start chatting</a><a href="/partners" class="btn btn-outline">Talk about a partnership</a></div></div></section>
</main>

<%- include('_partials/footer') %>
